.Dd March 29, 2026
.Dt PS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ps
.Nd display process status
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar auxleb
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
lists process information using Substrate's
.Xr sys_proc_list 2
and
.Xr sys_proc_info 2
interfaces.
The implementation is BSD-first:
the letters
.Cm a ,
.Cm u ,
.Cm x ,
.Cm l ,
.Cm e ,
and
.Cm b
may be given with or without a leading dash and may be clustered.
.Pp
The plain
.Nm
form prints a short, terminal-oriented listing.
.Cm ax
widens selection to all processes.
.Cm u
selects a user-oriented preset.
.Cm l
selects a long preset.
.Cm e
appends environment-oriented command tail rendering when available.
.Cm b
is a Substrate extension that inserts a
.Cm BITS
column showing process bitness.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm a
Include terminal-associated processes for all users.
.It Cm u
Use the user-oriented output preset.
.It Cm x
Include processes without restricting selection to the default terminal-oriented view.
.It Cm l
Use the long output preset.
.It Cm e
Append environment data after the command text when available.
.It Cm b
Insert a
.Cm BITS
column.
Valid values are
.Cm 16 ,
.Cm 32 ,
and
.Cm 64 .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ps
ps ax
ps aux
ps auxle
ps auxleb
.Ed
.Sh NOTES
The current kernel ABI exposes a larger
.Vt sys_procinfo_t
than the kernel currently populates fully.
Fields not yet populated by the kernel are rendered with stable fallbacks rather than guessed values.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sys_proc_info 2 ,
.Xr sys_proc_list 2
